    "description": "OBSERVED FEATURES & INVENTORY\nRock Specimen Collection:\nBoxed educational collection containing 15 individual rock specimens arranged in a compartmented tray.\nGeoscience Industries Material:\nInstruction sheet marked \"Geoscience Industries Ft. Collins, CO.\"\nCommon Metamorphic Rocks Theme:\nIncluded reference sheet titled \"Common Metamorphic Rocks.\"\nEducational Reference Materials:\nTwo printed study/reference sheets included covering metamorphic rock identification and changes during metamorphism.\nNumbered Specimens:\nSeveral rock samples retain numbered identification stickers.\nCompartmented Display Tray:\nWhite molded tray with individual specimen compartments.\nPresentation Box:\nHinged cardboard presentation/storage box included.\nVaried Rock Types:\nAssortment of specimens displaying different colors, textures, grain structures, and metamorphic characteristics.\nInstruction Sheet Content:\nReference material discusses foliated and non-foliated metamorphic rocks and associated classifications.\nComplete As Pictured:\nFifteen specimen compartments appear populated with rock samples as shown in the photographs.\nBox Dimensions:\nApproximately 11\" x 7\" x 1.5\".\nWeight:\nApproximately 1.395 lbs.\nPERCEIVED FLAWS & CONDITION NOTES\nUsed Educational Set:\nSet shows signs of previous handling, storage, and educational use.\nPaper Wear:\nReference sheets exhibit creasing, curling, wrinkles, edge wear, and storage-related wear.\nBox Wear:\nOuter box shows handling wear, edge wear, minor dents, and light discoloration.\nTray Dust:\nMinor dust, sediment, and loose rock particles visible within specimen compartments.\nLabel Wear:\nSome specimen identification stickers show age, wear, or discoloration.\nSpecimen Identification Unverified:\nIndividual rock identifications have not been independently verified beyond the included educational materials.\nNatural Imperfections:\nRock specimens contain natural fractures, uneven surfaces, inclusion